      "text": "<think>\nTo find the product of 444 and 981, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's how we can break it down step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 444 by 1 (the ones place of 981):**\n   \\[\n   444 \\times 1 = 444\n   \\]\n   Write down 444.\n\n2. **Multiply 444 by 8 (the tens place of 981), but remember to shift one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   444 \\times 8 = 3552\n   \\]\n   Shift 3552 one position to the left, making it 35520.\n\n3. **Multiply 444 by 9 (the hundreds place of 981), but remember to shift two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   444 \\times 9 = 4000\n   \\]\n   Shift 4000 two positions to the left, making it 400000.\n\n4. **Add all the results together:**\n   \\[\n   444 + 35520 + 400000 = 435964\n   \\]\n\nSo, the product of 444 and 981 is \\boxed{435964}.\n</think>\n<answer>\n435964\n</answer>",
