      "text": "<think>\nTo find the product of 548 and 607, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's how we can break it down step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 548 by 7 (the units digit of 607):**\n   - Multiply 548 by 7: \\( 548 \\times 7 = 3836 \\)\n   - Write down 3836 below the line.\n\n2. **Multiply 548 by 0 (the tens digit of 607), but remember to shift one place to the left:**\n   - Multiply 548 by 0: \\( 548 \\times 0 = 0 \\)\n   - Shift the result one place to the left: \\( 0 \\times 10 = 0 \\)\n   - Write down 0000 (or simply 0) below the previous result, shifted one place to the left.\n\n3. **Multiply 548 by 6 (the hundreds digit of 607), but remember to shift two places to the left:**\n   - Multiply 548 by 6: \\( 548 \\times 6 = 3288 \\)\n   - Shift the result two places to the left: \\( 3288 \\times 100 = 328800 \\)\n   - Write down 328800 below the previous results, shifted two places to the left.\n\n4. **Add all the results together:**\n   - \\( 3836 \\)\n   - \\( 0000 \\)\n   - \\( 328800 \\)\n   - Summing these values gives us \\( 3836 + 0 + 328800 = 332636 \\)\n\nTherefore, the product of 548 and 607 is \\(\\boxed{332636}\\).\n</think>\n<answer>\n332636\n</answer>",
